question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-957d23c2-2b79-5fed-9bde-ffd8c9acbe96"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-957d23c2-2b79-5fed-9bde-ffd8c9acbe96" :answer-field/id #uuid "957d23c2-2b79-5fed-9bde-ffd8c9acbe96" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-57b5ad0f-80e7-56c8-9312-0a0e7f64dea7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-57b5ad0f-80e7-56c8-9312-0a0e7f64dea7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57b5ad0f-80e7-56c8-9312-0a0e7f64dea7" :answer/id #uuid "57b5ad0f-80e7-56c8-9312-0a0e7f64dea7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3e3d6990-d239-54ed-b94a-9738925e98e2" :question/id #uuid "3e3d6990-d239-54ed-b94a-9738925e98e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-150762" :question/problem "![](images/46/46db75fc773bb1fbcb21817fe8371b855c8f9ac8a08e88134fa992dd68498982.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $m∠BAD={80}^{∘}.$ What equation could be used to find the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠BAC.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $∠BAC$ and $∠CAD$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(∠BAD)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(∠BAC$ and $∠CAD).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $∠BAC$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAD)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠CAD).$\n\nTherefore, the correct equation to determine $x$ is the following:\n\n$$\nx={80}^{∘}-{60}^{∘}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-715ee9db-17c4-5381-a913-c1d6ed279307"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-715ee9db-17c4-5381-a913-c1d6ed279307" :answer-field/id #uuid "715ee9db-17c4-5381-a913-c1d6ed279307" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/rad