he figure above, $m∠AOD={170}^{∘}$ and $m∠BOD={130}^{∘}.$ Find $m∠AOC.$" :question/worked-solution "The measure of $∠AOB$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠AOD)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠BOD).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nm∠AOB={170}^{∘}-{130}^{∘}={40}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLet's add this to our diagram:\n\n![](images/12/12431bb2f66402469571c49ac5637376f89e54265748fa88b3a6450c14bd7bce.png)\n\n  \n\nWe can now find the measure of $∠AOC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOC & =m∠AOB+m∠BOC \\\\  & ={40}^{∘}+{65}^{∘} \\\\  & ={105}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3f06001a-88ec-58d0-800a-3f395c862b10"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3f06001a-88ec-58d0-800a-3f395c862b10" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f06001a-88ec-58d0-800a-3f395c862b10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0ab2f952-ae64-5921-8621-f872d1bcf80e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0ab2f952-ae64-5921-8621-f872d1bcf80e" "answer-93f9fd6b-a694-5168-97ce-c9a7b439a6a4" "answer-6b95ac2c-aed5-57a4-9c97-6dd27cda5944" "answer-c3318d7a-e8df-5e9d-9938-8e9ff813fc7c" "answer-771a247a-4f56-50b2-9664-5bd5a8a2d794"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ab2f952-ae64-5921-8621-f872d1bcf80e" :answer/id #uuid "0ab2f952-ae64-5921-8621-f872d1bcf80e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{105}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93f9fd6b-a694-5168-97ce-c9a7b439a6a4" :answer/id #uuid "93f9fd6b-a694-5168-97ce-c9a7b439a6a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{110}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b95ac2c-aed5-57a4-9c97-6dd27cda5944" :answer/id #uuid "6b95ac2c-aed5-57a4-9c97-6dd27cda5944" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{115}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3318d7a-e8df-5e9d-9938-8e9ff813fc7c" :answer/id #uuid "c3318d7a-e8df-5e9d-9938-8e9ff813fc7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-771a247a-4f56-50b2-9664-5bd5a8a2d794" :answer/id #uuid "771a247a-4f56-50b2-9664-5bd5a8a2d794" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{95}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a93b6132-98b2-52ec-8ca3-233cb9c50ee1" :question/id #uuid "a93b6132-98b2-52ec-8ca3-233cb9c50ee1" :question/math-academy-id "q-154876" :question/problem "![](images/aa/aa5f7200cabc7aad7589c203d67dcbf81a6f632238369206e3845a89f25337c9.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $m∠BAE={120}^{∘}$ and $m∠BAD={80}^{∘}.$ Find $m∠CAE.$" :question/worked-solution "The measure of $∠DAE$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAE)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠BAD).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nm∠DAE={120}^{∘}-{80}^{∘}={40}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLet's add this to our diagram:\n\n![](images/df/df3e0be0d89947829ede0fbd55b19cb8d0a13c77cf5ece6c25933254d7cce29f.png)\n\nWe can now find the measure of $∠CAE:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CAE & =m∠CAD+m∠DAE \\\\  & ={60}^{∘}+{40}^{∘} \\\\  & ={100}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-76d6b294-b913-5ee6-9387-4ce663001aab"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76d6b294-b913-5ee6-9387-4ce663001aab" :answer-field/id #uuid "76d6b294-b913-5ee6-9387-4ce663001aab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cebbadd8-76fd-5742-8ba0-8466fa62e849" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cebbadd8-76fd-5742-8ba0-8466fa62e849" "answer-0fd9acdd-9fd8-534e-ae92-2b533b6f1435" "answer-48fdf3b5-2057-594f-84e9-26ee50f9ff83" "answer-060ae832-5075-56da-82fc-17a5809b5c48" "answer-75525703-7dca-57fe-a897-27f9b89f4f9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cebbadd8-76fd-5742-8ba0-8466fa62e849" :answer/id #uuid "cebbadd8-76fd-5742-8ba0-8466fa62e849" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{100}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f